              </span>
            </h2>

            <p>
              AIGO-OS can determine governance at different
              points in an AI-enabled process depending on
              the information and control interfaces exposed
              by connected systems.
            </p>
          </div>


          <div className={styles.momentGrid}>
            <article>
              <span>01</span>
              <h3>Before Action</h3>
              <p>
                Determine whether proposed activity may
                proceed under current governance conditions.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>02</span>
              <h3>During Workflow</h3>
              <p>
                Reassess governance when relevant context
                changes during an AI-enabled process.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>03</span>
              <h3>After Activity</h3>
              <p>
                Evaluate completed activity, preserve
                evidence and surface exceptions for review.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>


          <div className={styles.integrationBoundary}>
            <span>IMPORTANT IMPLEMENTATION BOUNDARY</span>

            <strong>
              AIGO-OS determines the governance response.
              Connected systems determine which technical
              enforcement actions are available.
            </strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>


      <section className={styles.controlledActionSection}>
        <div className={styles.shell}>
          <div className={styles.editorialGrid}>
            <div>
              <p className={styles.goldEyebrow}>
                CONTROLLED ACTION
              </p>

              <h2 className={styles.darkHeadline}>
                <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                  Turn governance decisions into actions
                </span>
                <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                  through connected systems.
                </span>
              </h2>
            </div>

            <div className={styles.darkCopy}>
              <p>
                A governance decision becomes operational
                when the appropriate response can be
                coordinated through available integrations.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>


          <div className={styles.actionWorkspace}>
            <article className={styles.actionDecision}>
              <span>GOVERNANCE DECISION</span>

              <strong>
                HUMAN AUTHORITY REQUIRED
              </strong>
            </article>


            <div className={styles.integrationActions}>
              {integrationActions.map((action) => (
                <span key={action}>
                  {action}
                </span>
              ))}
            </div>


            <article className={styles.connectedSystem}>
              <span>CONNECTED ENTERPRISE SYSTEM</span>

              <strong>
                Executes the available technical action
              </strong>

              <p>
                The actual enforcement or workflow change
                occurs through the relevant integrated
                platform.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>


          <p className={styles.lightStatement}>
            AIGO-OS orchestrates governance through
            integrations. It does not replace the enterprise
            systems that execute the underlying business
            process.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>


      <section className={styles.humanSection}>
        <div className={styles.shell}>
          <div className={styles.editorialGrid}>
            <div>
              <p className={styles.blueEyebrow}>
                HUMAN AUTHORITY
              </p>

              <h2 className={styles.lightHeadline}>
                <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                  Know when machine autonomy should
                </span>
                <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                  give way to accountable judgment.
                </span>
              </h2>
            </div>

            <div className={styles.lightCopy}>
              <p>
                Human oversight should not mean manually
                reviewing everything an AI system does.
              </p>

              <p>
                It should become meaningful when the
                situation requires authority, judgment or
                accountability that has not been delegated
                to the machine.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>


          <div className={styles.humanTransition}>
            <article>
              <span>01</span>
              <strong>AUTONOMOUS OPERATION</strong>
            </article>

            <div><span /></div>

            <article>
              <span>02</span>
              <strong>
                BUSINESS SIGNIFICANCE CHANGES
              </strong>
            </article>

            <div><span /></div>

            <article>
              <span>03</span>
              <strong>GOVERNANCE DECISION</strong>
            </article>

            <div><span /></div>

            <article className={styles.humanRequired}>
              <span>04</span>
              <strong>
                HUMAN AUTHORITY REQUIRED
              </strong>
            </article>


            <div className={styles.accountableRole}>
              <span>ACCOUNTABLE ROLE</span>
              <strong>PROCUREMENT DIRECTOR</strong>
              <small>
                Human decision intentionally unresolved on
                this page
              </small>
            </div>
          </div>


          <div className={styles.triggerGrid}>
            {humanTriggers.map((trigger) => (
              <span key={trigger}>
                {trigger}
              </span>
            ))}
          </div>


          <div className={styles.sectionAction}>
            <Link
              href="/product/human-authority"
              className={styles.secondaryButton}
            >
              Explore Human Authority
            </Link>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>


      <section className={styles.reassessmentSection}>
        <div className={styles.shell}>
          <div className={styles.editorialGrid}>
            <div>
              <p className={styles.goldEyebrow}>
                CONTINUOUS REASSESSMENT
              </p>

              <h2 className={styles.darkHeadline}>
                <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                  A governance decision is valid for
                </span>
                <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                  the context that produced it.
                </span>
              </h2>
            </div>

            <div className={styles.darkCopy}>
              <p>
                Enterprise context changes. Authority,
                supplier status, policy, risk and available
                evidence can change with it.
              </p>

              <p>
                When material context changes, AIGO-OS can
                reassess the situation using the updated
                information available through integrations.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>


          <div className={styles.timelineWorkspace}>
            <div className={styles.timelineControls}>
              {(
                Object.keys(
                  timeline,
                ) as TimelineKey[]
              ).map((key) => (
                <button
                  key={key}
                  type="button"
                  onClick={() =>
                    setTimelineState(key)
                  }
                  className={
                    timelineState === key
                      ? styles.timelineButtonActive
                      : styles.timelineButton
                  }
                >
                  <span>{timeline[key].time}</span>
                  <strong>
                    {timeline[key].decision}
                  </strong>
                </button>
              ))}
            </div>


            <article className={styles.timelineContext}>
              <span>
                CONTEXT AT {activeTimeline.time}
              </span>

              <dl>
                <div>
                  <dt>Payment</dt>
                  <dd>{activeTimeline.payment}</dd>
                </div>

                <div>
                  <dt>Supplier state</dt>
                  <dd>{activeTimeline.supplier}</dd>
                </div>

                <div>
                  <dt>Context change</dt>
                  <dd>{activeTimeline.context}</dd>
                </div>

                <div>
                  <dt>Business Significance</dt>
                  <dd>{activeTimeline.significance}</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
            </article>


            <article
              className={`${styles.timelineDecision} ${
                activeTimeline.tone === "continue"
                  ? styles.timelineContinue
                  : activeTimeline.tone === "reassess"
                    ? styles.timelineReassess
                    : activeTimeline.tone === "control"
                      ? styles.timelineControl
                      : styles.timelineBlocked
              }`}
            >
              <span>GOVERNANCE DECISION</span>

              <strong>
                {activeTimeline.decision}
              </strong>
            </article>
          </div>


          <p className={styles.lightStatement}>
            Continuous governance requires the ability to
            reconsider decisions when material context
            changes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>


      <section className={styles.evidenceSection}>
        <div className={styles.shell}>
          <div className={styles.sectionIntro}>
            <p className={styles.blueEyebrow}>
              DECISION HISTORY
            </p>

            <h2>
              <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                Preserve the basis of governance
              </span>
              <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                decisions as evidence.
              </span>
            </h2>

            <p>
              Governance does not end when a decision is
              made. AIGO-OS carries the decision context
              forward toward Governance Receipts.
            </p>
          </div>


          <div className={styles.evidenceFlow}>
            <article>
              <span>ACTOR PASSPORT</span>
              <strong>Procurement Agent 07</strong>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>MACHINE AUTHORITY</span>
              <strong>MA-2041</strong>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>BUSINESS SIGNIFICANCE</span>
              <strong>High</strong>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>GOVERNANCE DECISION</span>
              <strong>
                Human Authority Required
              </strong>
            </article>

            <article className={styles.futureEvidence}>
              <span>HUMAN DECISION</span>
              <strong>Approved with condition</strong>
            </article>

            <article className={styles.receiptPreview}>
              <span>GOVERNANCE RECEIPT</span>
              <strong>GR-84291</strong>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>


      <section className={styles.roleSection}>
        <div className={styles.shell}>
          <div className={styles.sectionIntro}>
            <p className={styles.goldEyebrow}>
              THE AIGO-OS GOVERNANCE MODEL
            </p>

            <h2 className={styles.darkRoleTitle}>
              <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                Turn understanding into an
              </span>
              <span className={styles.keepLine}>
                operational governance response.
              </span>
            </h2>
          </div>


          <div className={styles.platformRail}>
            {platformStages.map((stage, index) => (
              <div
                key={stage}
                className={
                  index === 3
                    ? styles.platformStageActive
                    : index < 3
                      ? styles.platformStageComplete
                      : styles.platformStage
                }
              >
                <span>
                  {String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
                </span>

                <strong>{stage}</strong>

                {index < 3 && (
                  <small>Established context</small>
                )}

                {index === 3 && (
                  <small>Current capability</small>
                )}

                {index === 4 && (
                  <small>Next capability</small>
                )}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>


      <section className={styles.finalCta}>
        <div className={styles.finalGlow} />

        <div className={styles.finalInner}>
          <p className={styles.blueEyebrow}>
            GOVERNANCE DECISIONING
          </p>

          <h2>
            <span className={styles.keepLine}>
              Apply the governance the situation
            </span>
            <span className={styles.keepLine}>
              actually requires.
            </span>
          </h2>

          <p>
            Use persistent actor identity, delegated Machine
            Authority, Business Significance and applicable
            enterprise requirements to determine the
            appropriate governance response to AI activity.
          </p>

          <div className={styles.heroActions}>
            <Link
              href="/demo"
              className={styles.primaryButton}
            >
              Request a Demo
            </Link>

            <Link
              href="/product/human-authority"
              className={styles.secondaryButton}
            >
              Explore Human Authority
            </Link>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  );
}
